WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.785
Passive monitoring observes existing communication without sending probes or commands to the monitored devices.

00:00:06.785 --> 00:00:16.633
This approach is often preferred in OT because some legacy controllers, protocol stacks, and embedded devices are sensitive to unexpected traffic.

00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:21.667
Visibility should not create an avoidable production or safety risk.

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:29.764
A network tap can provide a copy of traffic while remaining electrically isolated from the monitored path.

00:00:29.764 --> 00:00:40.488
A switch SPAN or mirror port can also copy selected traffic to a sensor, though configuration, capacity, and switch behavior must be reviewed.

00:00:40.488 --> 00:00:48.586
Sensors should be placed where they can observe meaningful flows without becoming part of the control path.

00:00:48.586 --> 00:00:54.933
Passive collection can identify devices, protocols, communication pairs, timing, and some command types.

00:00:54.933 --> 00:01:03.906
It is particularly useful around control-area boundaries, industrial DMZs, remote-access gateways, and links between site operations and lower-level networks.

00:01:03.906 --> 00:01:06.313
Passive monitoring has limits.

00:01:06.313 --> 00:01:17.037
It may not see dormant assets, serial networks, encrypted content, traffic on an unobserved switch, or activity that occurs entirely within a device.

00:01:17.037 --> 00:01:23.384
Asset inventory, host logs, vendor records, configuration review, and physical verification remain necessary.

00:01:23.384 --> 00:01:25.791
Deployment requires engineering coordination.

00:01:25.791 --> 00:01:33.889
Confirm that taps, mirror ports, sensors, power, and management connections do not interfere with redundancy or timing.

00:01:33.889 --> 00:01:43.737
Secure the monitoring platform itself, separate its management path, restrict access to captured data, and define what happens if collection stops.

00:01:43.737 --> 00:01:47.895
The principle is observe safely and interpret carefully.

00:01:47.895 --> 00:01:58.182
Passive evidence reduces blind spots, but it does not automatically prove that an asset is secure or that every action is authorized.

00:01:58.182 --> 00:02:04.528
Monitoring becomes reliable when its coverage, limitations, ownership, and operational assumptions are documented.
